>>
Rule 1 (input must be a tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (out tensor, if provided, must have the same dtype as input to avoid illegal casts)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (out tensor, if provided, must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 6 (out, when used, must be a tensor)
{v_2 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 8 (out must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
